[0.007, "o", "CONCLUSION: bd-38 makes an unhinted provider usage-limit 429 cool the provider for ~6 h (a hinted reset still wins), escalate 6 h -> 12 h -> 24 h on repeats, stay visible to other fleet processes through the shared file, and make the fallback loop skip the exhausted provider without spawning a second process or minting a new -fallback-N session.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\nEverything below is executed, not quoted. Every write goes to a scratch cooldown file\r\nunder /tmp (BELAYD_MODEL_COOLDOWN_FILE); nothing under ~/.pi is written.\r\n"]
